quran[10]{c,v,t}:
  11,72,"She said: ‘Amazing! Shall I bear a child when I am an extremely old woman, and this husband of mine is an extremely older man? That would indeed be an astonishing thing!’*"
  11,73,"They said: ‘Are you astonished at the command of Allah? The mercy of Allah and His blessings be upon you, O People of the House! Indeed, He is the Praiseworthy, the Glorious.’"
  11,74,"So when the fear had left Ibrahim (Abraham), and the glad tidings had come to him, he began to plead with Us for the people of Lut (Lot)."
  11,75,"Ibrahim (Abraham) was forbearing, highly plaintive and devoutly repentant."
  11,76,"(The angels said:) ‘O Ibrahim (Abraham)! Turn away from this (pleading). Indeed, the command of your Lord has come, and an irrevocable punishment shall overtake them.’"
  11,77,"And when Our messengers came to Lut (Lot), he was distressed for them and felt himself in a difficult situation for their sake. And he said: ‘This is a terrible day!’"
  11,78,"Then his people came to him, running towards him, and they had already been committing evil deeds. He said: ‘O my people! These are my (people’s) daughters. They are purer (i.e. lawful) for you (through marriage). So be wary of Allah and do not disgrace me regarding my guests. Is there not a sensible man among you?’"
  11,79,They said: ‘You surely know that we have no claim to your (people’s) daughters. And you very well know what we desire.’
  11,80,"He said: ‘If only I had the strength to resist you, or I could seek refuge in some mighty support!’"
  11,81,"They said: ‘O Lut (Lot)! We are the messengers of your Lord. They shall never reach you. Travel with your family (and followers) in the dark of the night (leaving the town), and none of you shall turn back except your wife. The same (disaster) will afflict her as will afflict the others. Indeed, their appointed time (for the punishment) is the dawn. Is not the dawn (already) near?’"
